{"d":22,"passage":{"title":"理想国","author":"Plato (B. Jowett trans.)","text":"Neither is it easy to give a definite answer to any one who asks how he is to improve. He may study from the speculative side the profession or business in which he is practically engaged. He may make Homer, Dante, Shakespeare, Plato, Bacon the friends and companions of his life. He may select for enquiry some point of history or some unexplained phenomenon of nature. An hour a day passed in such scientific or literary pursuits will furnish as many facts as the memory can retain, and will give him 'a pleasure not to be repented of' (Timaeus). Only let him beware of being the slave of crotchets, or of running after a Will o' the Wisp in his ignorance, or in his vanity of attributing to himself the gifts of a poet or assuming the air of a philosopher. Better to build up the mind by slow additions, to creep on quietly from one thing to another, to gain insensibly new powers and new interests in knowledge, than to form vast schemes which are never destined to be realized."},"words":[{"w":"outsourcing","uk":"'ajt,sɔːsiŋ","us":"/'ajt,sɔsiŋ/","p":"","m":"[计] 外部资源利用","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"adjustable","uk":"ə'dʒʌstəbl","us":"/ə'dʒʌstəbl/","p":"adj.","m":"a. 可调节的 [电] 可调整的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"michelle","uk":"mɪ'ʃɛl","us":"/mɪ'ʃɛl/","p":"","m":"n. 米歇尔（女子名）","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"alphabetical","uk":".ælfə'betikəl","us":"/.ælfə'betikəl/","p":"adj.","m":"a. 依字母顺序的, 字母的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"aaron","uk":"'eərən","us":"/'ɛrən/","p":"","m":"n. 亚伦（男子名）；[圣经]亚伦（摩西之兄, 犹太教的第一祭司长）","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":{"r":"Exodus 5:4","c":"出埃及记 5:4","t":"And the king of Egypt said unto them, Wherefore do ye, Moses and Aaron, let the people from their works? get you unto your burdens."}},{"w":"handheld","uk":"hændheld","us":"/hændheld/","p":"","m":"a. 掌上型；手持型","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"f